  "final_text": "**Wartapak (Poznań) has the lowest price, but it isn't the cheapest delivered.** Only Rednitz (Nürnberg) quoted delivered to your plant, which is what your request asked for. Wartapak and Kartovka quote pickup at their own sites, so you would pay the freight on top. Their offers can't be compared fairly until you know that cost.\n\n**Cost per year for 40,000 boxes, before freight**\n\n| | A · Rednitz | B · Wartapak | C · Kartovka |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Price per box | 0.66 € | 0.52 € (520 €/1,000) | 0.575 € (57.50 €/100) |\n| One-time tooling | none | 1,450 € | none |\n| **Per year** | **26,400 €** | **22,250 €** | **23,000 €** |\n| Per year, paying early for the discount | 25,872 € (2 %) | 21,834 € (2 %, not on tooling) | 22,310 € (3 %) |\n| Delivery | **to your plant** | pickup in Poznań | pickup in Brno |\n\n**What changes the picture**\n\n- **Freight.** Both foreign suppliers are roughly 700 km away. B saves about 4,000 € a year against A, and C saves about 3,500 €. Judging from C's figure of 10,000 boxes = 10 pallets, that comes to:\n  - **B** must order at least 20,000 boxes at a time, so two trips of about 20 pallets each. B is only cheaper if each trip costs less than about 2,000 €. A real truck quote could get close to that.\n  - **C** delivers in lots of 10,000, so four trips of about 10 pallets each. C is only cheaper if each trip costs less than about 850–900 €.\n- **Paper surcharge (C).** If the paper price index rises between order and delivery, Kartovka adds 60 % of that rise to the price. A 10 % rise adds about 0.035 € per box, and the surcharge gets no early-payment discount. The quote is also only valid until 15 Nov 2026, so the price isn't fixed for 2027.\n- **Price validity (B).** The quote is only valid until 30 Nov 2026 and promises no fixed price for the year. Rednitz guarantees its price for orders up to 31 Dec 2027.\n- **Storage (B).** Taking 20,000 boxes at once means about 20 pallets in your warehouse and money tied up in stock. Rednitz delivers from 3,000 boxes, five working days after you order.\n\n**My recommendation:** Rednitz is the only offer whose full cost you actually know. Before deciding, ask Wartapak and Kartovka for a price delivered to your plant (as your request asked) and a fixed price for 2027. Otherwise, get a freight quote for 20-pallet loads from Poznań. If it comes in well under 2,000 € per trip, Wartapak is the cheapest. If not, Rednitz is.\n\nThe freight limits are estimates based on 1,000 boxes per pallet. All prices are net of VAT.",
